{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531055-w20-tribes-merits-and-gifts","id":1531055,"title":"W20 Tribes, Merits and Gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-18T06:17:04-08:00","id":1531055,"title":"W20 Tribes, Merits and Gifts","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Some questions about W20 merits interacting with Gifts, merit validity and more:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The <b>Acute Sense</b> merit lowers the difficulty of all tasks using the sense. If I get <b>Acute Sense (Smell)</b>, do I get a lowered difficulty in gifts like <b>Scent of the True Form</b>? Or <b>Acute Sense (Hearing)</b>, lowered difficulty on <b>Beat of the Heart-Drum</b>?</li> <li>Are Merits from non-W20 books still valid? <b>Friend of Sorcery</b> or<b> Born Leader</b> from Rage against the Heavens for example.</li> <li>Are rules from non-W20 books still valid? For example, Uktena Revised had a Medicine Bag talisman, a non-fetish item that could grant an extra willpoint dot, is this still valid?</li> <li>Do Stargazers count as part of the Hengeyokai? Can they benefit of the Beast Courts gifts lists and Auspices?</li> <li>Does the Totem count as a Pack member for purposes of the<b> Pack Mentality</b> flaw? If so, does it have to be visible in the physical world?</li> </ol>Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-24-2024, 05:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T06:28:32-08:00","id":1531056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1531055-w20-tribes-merits-and-gifts#post1531055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> Some questions about W20 merits interacting with Gifts, merit validity and more:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The <b>Acute Sense</b> merit lowers the difficulty of all tasks using the sense. If I get <b>Acute Sense (Smell)</b>, do I get a lowered difficulty in gifts like <b>Scent of the True Form</b>? Or <b>Acute Sense (Hearing)</b>, lowered difficulty on <b>Beat of the Heart-Drum</b>?</li> <li>Are Merits from non-W20 books still valid? <b>Friend of Sorcery</b> or<b> Born Leader</b> from Rage against the Heavens for example.</li> <li>Are rules from non-W20 books still valid? For example, Uktena Revised had a Medicine Bag talisman, a non-fetish item that could grant an extra willpoint dot, is this still valid?</li> <li>Do Stargazers count as part of the Hengeyokai? Can they benefit of the Beast Courts gifts lists and Auspices?</li> </ol>Thanks</div> </div> </div> </div>1. If I'm your ST? Then sure.<br /> 2. Anything from Revised works pretty much perfectly in W20 so as an ST I'd have no issue with anything being used from Revised books. 2nd Ed and 1st would probably need some adjustment.<br /> 3. Again...as an ST Sure. No worries.<br /> 4. Anyone who has joined the Beast Courts can use BC Gift Lists and Auspices. So those Stargazers that have done so absolutely can. Not all Stargazers have joined the BC though so its a case by case basis. Same for Steppes Striders, Scarlet Claws, possibly some members of House Blood Red Crest, a smattering of Firehair Fianna and other Garou populations throughout Asia.<br /> <br /> If your looking for official word there isn't any but I honestly see zero reason to not use Revised books in conjunction with W20...........in many cases ( looks sideways at Kinfolk:ABA and Changing Ways) the Revised counterparts are far, far superior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-18T10:30:17-08:00","id":1531061,"title":"","content":"In general, I'm going to echo Damian's takeaway: Revised and W20 are exceedingly compatible, so unless there's a good reason, I mix and match.<br /> <br /> 1) I'm a bit less for this. On one hand, a lot of Gifts have difficulties that are far too high, so letting some bonuses like this count is a way to counter that. On the other hand there's a lot of these Merits (not just Acute Senses) that can get you a -1 or -2 for fairly broad groups of Gifts and it can make players really chase Merits for that over flavor. I think paying attention to wording is important too.<br /> <br /> 2) There are some that have W20 versions with different names, so I'd default to those, but otherwise yes.<br /> <br /> 3) Again, there are going to be exceptions, but generally, I allow this as well.<br /> <br /> 4) Stargazers that are part of the Garou Nation aren't part of the Beast Courts. Gotta pick one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T07:06:22-08:00","id":1531113,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar479_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"479\" data-vbnamecard=\"479\">Damian May</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> thank you both for your answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T14:13:42-07:00","id":1533089,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar479_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"479\" data-vbnamecard=\"479\">Damian May</a>and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a><br /> A new question, I did not want to open a new thread for it (but I may).<br /> <br /> Does the Totem count as a Pack member for purposes of the<b> Pack Mentality</b> flaw? If so, does it have to be visible in the physical world?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T14:35:36-07:00","id":1533091,"title":"","content":"I would think the Totem Avatar doesn't count as a pack member.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-24T15:13:59-07:00","id":1533092,"title":"","content":"While I would consider the spirit part of the pack in a general sense, I don't generally allow it to be a &quot;packmate&quot; and interact with this kind of Flaw or things like Pack Tactics unless the mechanics of something specifically say otherwise; just like kinfolk might be seen as part of a pack in a broad sense, mechanics that interact with packmates don't count them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-26T15:57:36-07:00","id":1533214,"title":"","content":"While I do think one can argue that the pack totem is a member of the pack itself, I do not think the writers of the Pack Mentality Flaw considered including the pack totem for the purposes of the Flaw. So as ST I would not count it as a pack member for the purposes of the Flaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T14:09:35-07:00","id":1534778,"title":"","content":"Another Stargazers question for the thread <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar479_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"479\" data-vbnamecard=\"479\">Damian May</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a><br /> <br /> Every other tribe write up in the W20 core, explicitly states which backgrounds are <b>Discouraged </b>or <b>Restricted</b>; but the Stargazer description is more of a suggestion noting that &quot;<i>Stargazers with Fetish or Resources are rare; they also avoid the emotional bonds of Allies when they can</i>\u200b&quot;. Are those 3 Backgrounds Restricted, Discouraged or simply not suggested for the tribe?\u200b<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-26T14:30:51-07:00","id":1534779,"title":"","content":"I think there was an editing error. The two page Tribe write up doesn't specify it, but the character creation chart on page 113 lists all three as Discouraged. While there is a bit of a discrepancy as the larger write-ups include Background restrictions with the Discouraged and Restricted verbiage to be clear, it really don't make sense for the chart to be wrong.<br /> <br /> The whole point of adding the Discouraged category to the game was to address either Restricted Backgrounds that don't make sense and lead to all sorts of weird things in past editions (Bone Gnawers used to be Restricted from Resources, so no Bone Gnawer could ever get Resources, even in play, which lead to a whole convoluted mess of trying to justify how a whole Tribe was just magically bad with money except for a few that had a Merit), or things like the Stargazers were as a Tribe they don't like certain Backgrounds but they weren't Restricted because it was understood that many would put the practical benefits over Tribal philosophy.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I would consider the chart right, and the full write-up an oversight for not using &quot;Discouraged&quot; specifically in the text like it should have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}